[ti:Week02-Thur.mp3]

[00:00.00]blend 熟义 v. （使）混合，（使）混杂‖n. 混合； 混合物 示例 ① Motorists face a potential rise in fuel costs equivalent to almost 3p a litre as oil companies increase the blend of ethanol in petrol to meet EU sustainability targets, according to research published today. 今日发布的调查显示，为实现欧盟可持续发展的目标，汽油公司会在汽油和乙醇的混合物中增加乙醇的含量。因此车主可能会面临油价上涨，上涨幅度约为每升三英镑。（The Times） ② Our music blends traditional and modern styles. 我们的音乐融合了传统和现代风格。
[00:11.35]confront 熟义 v. 面临，遭遇；处理，解决；面对，（与某人）对质 示例 ① And how does it compare with the other, seemingly perpetual health scares we confront, like panic over lead in synthetic athletic fields? 另外，和其他危险 ——那些看起来永远无法摆脱的恐慌，例如人造运动场含铅过量问题相比又如何呢？（2009. 12）② This was the first time she had confronted a robber. 这是她第一次面对劫匪。
[00:19.88]detail 熟义 n. 琐事；细节，详情；[pl.] 资料，消息 ‖v. 详述 示例 ① One should create a solid statement in a dozen or so sentences that describe in detail how they see their life related to work. 一个人应该创造出几句坚定的宣言，具体描述怎样把生活同工作联系起来。（2007. 6）② This question will be discussed in more detail in the next chapter. 这个问题将在下一章详细论述。
[00:28.11]budget 熟义 n. 预算‖v. 把…编入预算 示例 ① It can also provide competitive advantage, especially when small businesses want to attract new staff but don't have the budget to offer huge salaries. 在家办公还能提高企业的竞争优势，特别是那些想吸引新员工但又付不起大笔薪酬的小型企业。（2009. 12）② This plan has been budgeted at ten million francs. 这个计划已制定了1000万法郎的预算。
[00:36.73]ozone 熟义 n. 臭氧 示例 ① Last week scientists convened by the United Nations Environment Program unveiled satellite data showing summertime ozone loss of 3 percent in the 1980s. 上周，联合国环境规划署召集的科学家们公开的卫星数据显示，20世纪80年代的夏季，臭氧减少了3%。（Newsweek） ② Over the past few years, we have been constantly speaking about ozone holes, droughts, about food contaminated with chemicals. 在过去的几年中，我们一直在谈论臭氧层空洞、干旱还有化学物质对于食物的污染。
[00:48.05]occasion 熟义 n. …的时候；特别的事情（或仪式、庆典）；适当的机会，时机 示例 ① On occasions it is the fear that certain disclosures may be unacceptable to family or friends that motivates an individual to seek professional help. 有时，正是因为担心某些事情不能对家人和朋友讲，才使一个人去寻求专业帮助。（2012. 12）② The manager has been known on occasion to lose his temper. 大家都知道经理有时候会发脾气。
[00:57.07]farewell 熟义 n. 告别，辞行‖int. 再见，再会 示例 ① On Facebook's fifth anniversary, a not-so-fond farewell. 脸谱网第五届周年庆是并不太令人喜爱的欢送会。（Newsweek） ② He said his farewell and left. 他告别后就离开了。
[01:01.85]restore 熟义 v. 恢复（某种情况或感受）；重新采用 （或实施） 示例 ① Of course one alternative to this is to restore capital punishment, but I'm not sure I would be for that. 当然，其中一个解决这个问题的可选方案是恢复死刑，但是我不确定我支持这么做。（2008. 6）② His job is restoring old paintings. 他的工作是修复旧画。
[01:08.58]mostly 熟义 ad. 主要地，一般地，通常 示例 ① Younger people today mostly accept that they will have to work for longer and that their pensions will be less generous. 现在，年轻人大多能接受以下现实：他们的工作年限会更长，而得到的养老金却更少。（2010. 12）② They are mostly out on Sundays. 他们星期天一般不在家。
[01:15.38]germ 熟义 n. 微生物，细菌，病菌 示例 ① "Germs are spread by hands," she explains. “病菌通过手来传播。”她解释说。（Times） ② Disinfectant can kill germs. 消毒剂可以杀菌。
[01:19.06]trace 熟义 v. 查出；追溯‖n. 痕迹，遗迹 示例 ① A group of researchers reveal scores of studies that trace the relationship between health and interaction with others. 一组研究学者透露了追踪健康和与人交流两者之间关系的大量研究。（2010. 6）② He can trace his family tree back to the 17th century. 他家的家谱能追溯到17世纪。
[01:26.35]genuine 熟义 a. 真实的，名副其实的 示例 ① Dan Clancy, the chief architect of Google Books, does seem genuine in his conviction that this is primarily a philanthropic exercise. 谷歌图书的总设计师丹•克兰西，似乎确实深信不疑地认为，这主要是一项慈善之举。（2011. 12） ② This painting is a genuine Picasso. 这幅画是毕加索的真迹。
[01:33.67]destructive 熟义 a. 引起破坏（或毁灭）的，破坏（或毁灭）性的 示例 ① America is a competitive society; our kids need to adjust to that, but too much pushiness can be destructive. 美国是个竞争激烈的社会，我们的孩子要学会适应它，但是太多的逼迫会带来毁灭性的后果。（2008. 6）② This is the destructive power of modern weapons. 这是现代武器的毁灭性力量。
[01:41.25]impatient 熟义 a. 不耐烦的，没有耐心的；急于，热切期待 示例 ① I am, however, growing impatient for an iPad app, which should better display this information for a larger screen. 然而，我却越发急于得到一个iPad应用程序，这样就能在更大的屏幕上更好地呈现此信息。（American Today） ② He is impatient with his son. 他对他儿子没有耐心。
[01:48.51]drift 熟义 n. 流动；水流；意义‖v. 漂流，漂移 示例 ① As the nation moves further into the Obama presidency, will politically engaged young people continue to support the president and his agenda, or will they gradually drift away? 随着奥巴马开始执政，那些关心政治的年轻人是会继续支持他们的总统及其工作议程，还是会逐渐远离呢？（2010. 6） ② Do you catch her drift? 你明白她什么意思了吗？
[01:57.10]specify 熟义 v. 具体说明，详述 示例 ① The contract for the purchase of the property did not specify a completion date. 房屋的购买合同没有明确指定一个完结日期。（The Times）② You must specify your size when ordering clothes. 订购服装的时候，你一定要详细说明你要的号码。
[02:03.05]hunt 熟义 v. 打猎；搜寻；追捕‖n. 搜寻；打猎 示例 ① What's hot for 2007 among the very rich? A $7.3 million diamond ring. A trip to Tanzania to hunt wild animals. 2007年富豪们最热门的话题是什么？价值 730万美金的钻戒。坦桑尼亚狩猎之旅。（2007. 12） ② He is still hunting for a new job. 他还在找新工作。
[02:09.59]revolve 熟义 v. 旋转，环绕，转动 示例 ① Much of the national discussion about school reform revolves around recruiting and keeping top talent in the teaching field. 关于学校改革的全国性讨论大部分都是围绕招聘顶尖级人才并将他们留在教育领域这一话题。（The Washington Post） ② The discussion revolved around the question of changing the party's theme. 讨论的中心问题是改变派对的主题。
[02:18.34]military 熟义 a. 军事的，军队的‖n. 军人，军队 示例 ① The Pentagon built the network for military contractors and universities doing military research to exchange information. 美国国防部为军事任务承包商和进行军事研究的大学构建了这个网络，以便交换信息。（2009. 6） ② We may have to take military action against this area. 我们可能不得不对这一地区采取军事行动。
[02:26.38]crisis 熟义 n. 危机，危急关头；危难时刻，病危期 示例 ① In a report entitled "Averting the Old Age Crisis", it argued that pension arrangements in most countries were unsustainable. 一篇名为《转变老年危机》 的报告中提到，大部分国家的养老金发放计划都是不可持续的。（2010. 12） ② In time of crisis, he knows which friends he can turn to. 在危难关头，他知道能投靠哪些朋友。
[02:34.48]expire 熟义 v.（因到期而）失效；届满；去世 示例 ① The Bush-era tax cuts are set to expire at year end. 布什时代的减税政策年底要到期了。（The New York Times）② His term of office expires at the end of July. 他的任期七月底届满。
[02:39.36]mingle 熟义 v.（使）与…结合；（尤指在社交场所）相交往 示例 ① It is early afternoon, and the smells of dirty diapers and grease mingle in the bleak Minneapolis apartment. 时间是下午的早些时候，脏尿布和油脂的味道混合着弥漫在明尼阿波里斯市一间阴冷的公寓里。（Time）② She felt a kind of happiness mingled with regret. 她既高兴又遗憾。
[02:46.58]outbreak 熟义 n. （暴力、疾病等坏事的）爆发，突然发生 示例 ① It started as what seemed like a lethal outbreak in Mexico, and then spread north of the border. 起初这种流行病看起来好像是一种爆发于墨西哥的致死病，接下来传播到北部边界。（Scientific American）② Outbreaks of rain are expected in the evening. 晚上将有暴雨。
[02:53.61]preference 熟义 n. 偏爱；偏爱的事物 示例 ① It reflects Americans' preference for imported goods. 这反映了美国人对进口商品的偏好。（2011. 12） ② He expressed a strong preference for the original plan. 他强烈表示喜欢原计划。
[02:58.68]organic 熟义 a. 有机的；有机物的；器官的 示例 ① This in a city that requires school cafeterias to serve organic meals. 这发生在一个要求学校食堂提供有机食物的城市。（2009. 12）② People improve the soil by adding organic matter. 人们加入有机物以改良土壤。
[03:04.28]normally 熟义 ad. 通常，正常情况下；正常地；平常地 示例 ① The small gravitational pull created by the rotating space city would allow space-tourists and residents to walk around and function normally within the structure. 旋转的太空城市所产生的小型重力场使太空游客和居民可以在建筑内自由行走和正常活动。（2006. 12）② His heart is beating normally. 他心跳正常。
[03:12.54]benign 熟义 a. 善良的，和善的 示例 ① And even apparently benign chemicals may combine to produce toxic effects greater than the sum of their individual effects. 而且甚至是表面看起来良性的化学物质混合后也可能产生毒性作用， 这种毒性作用比它们个体的毒性作用加在一起还要强。（New Scientist） ② He is very benign. 他很善良。
[03:19.51]deadly 熟义 a.（可能）致命的；彻底的；非常有效的；枯燥的‖ad. 极其，非常 示例 ① Without the atmosphere, we would be forced to seek shelters, as there would be nothing to protect us from the sun's deadly rays. 没有这种环境，我们将被迫寻找藏身处，否则我们将裸露在太阳致命的光线下失去保护。（2012. 12） ② He sat in deadly silence. 他默不作声地坐着。
[03:26.93]virtually 熟义 ad. 几乎，差不多 示例 ① There's virtually no limit to how much of that can be saved, as prototype "zero-energy homes" in Switzerland and Germany have shown. 实际上在这方面可能节约的能源数量是无穷无尽的，就像瑞士和德国的“零耗能家庭”样板房所展示的那样。（2007. 12）② Virtually all students can be exempt from the tax. 差不多所有的学生都能免此税项。
[03:35.03]imitate 熟义 v. 模仿，仿效 示例 ① These neurons appear to help humans imitate the behaviours they observe. 这些神经元似乎帮助人类模仿他们观察到的行为。（Scientific American）② His style of painting has been imitated by other artists. 他的绘画风格为其他画家所模仿。
[03:41.11]formula 熟义 n. 公式；分子式；方案 示例 ① His first lecture was delivered on Nov. 4, 1915, and it explained his new approach, though he admitted he did not yet have the precise mathematical formulation of it. 他的第一次演说在1915年 11月4日发布，虽然他承认他还没有关于它的精确的数学公式，但是他还是在演说中解释了他的新方法。（2007. 12）② We're trying to work out a peace formula acceptable to both sides in the dispute. 我们正在设法制定出一个争执双方都可以接受的和平方案。
[03:51.65]barely 熟义 ad. 仅仅；几乎不；刚好 示例 ① A year later barely half of the 20,000 cards had been issued. 一年后两万张绿卡颁发了几乎不到一半。（2008. 6）② He was barely able to stand. 他勉强能站立。
[03:55.88]emit 熟义 v. 发出，散发（光、热、声音、气等） 示例 ① Our air quality now suffers from the effects of pollutants emitted directly from our cars. 现在我们的空气质量受到从汽车直接排放出的污染物的影响。（2008. 12）② The volcano emitted the sulphur gases. 火山喷发出硫酸气体。
[04:01.84]salvation 熟义 n. 得救，救世；（危险、灾难、损失等的）避免方式 示例 ① The right rejects the idea that sometimes government must rescue the economy from panic; the left sees salvation only in ever-larger government. 右翼反对政府有时必须挽救经济于恐慌的观点；而左翼则认为拯救经济全靠日益强大的政府。（Newsweek）② Group therapy classes have been his self-salvation. 他一直靠参加集体治疗班来自救。
[04:10.72]fake 熟义 a. 假的‖n. 假货，赝品‖v. 伪造，冒充 示例 ① If you're like most people, you've indulged in fake listening many times. 如果你像大多数人一样，你已经放纵自己，假装听课许多次了。（2007. 12）② This painting was proved to be a fake. 这幅画结果证实是赝品。
[04:16.28]descend 熟义 v. 下降；下倾；降临 示例 ① Ultimately we must get a handle on those issues as well, or a creature that outlived the dinosaurs will meet its end at the hands of humans, leaving our descendants to wonder how creature so ugly could have won so much affection. 最终我们也一定要解决那些问题，否则这些比恐龙幸存时间还长的生物就将在人类的手上灭绝，我们的后代会好奇为什么如此丑陋的生物居然能够获得那么多的关爱？（2009. 6） ② This country was descending into chaos. 这个国家陷入一片混乱。
[04:27.25]merge 熟义 v.（使）合并，结合；相融 示例 ① "The big trend is that technology is merging with fashion," Vitagliano said. "We know finding the right denim can be a complicated process, and we want our customers to know that we have a fun solution." 维塔利亚诺说：“科技与时尚融合是大势所趋，我们知道找到合适的牛仔布可能会是一个复杂的过程，我们想让顾客知道我们有一个有趣的解决方案。”（The Washington Post） ② Her department will be merged with mine. 她的部门将和我部门的合并。
[04:37.82]anticipate 熟义 v. 预料，预期；预见；期盼 示例 ① Unlike the Americans, the Europeans failed to anticipate how the markets would react to their endless borrowing. 与美国人不同，欧洲人没能预见到他们不停的借债会导致市场作何反应。（2012. 6）② He anticipated that sales will rise next year. 他预计明年销售量将会增加。
[04:44.88]currency 熟义 n. 通货，货币；通用，流行 示例 ① The weak dollar is a source of humiliation, for a nation's self-esteem rests in part on the strength of its currency. 疲软的美元带来了耻辱，因为一个国家的自尊部分在于其货币的势能。（2008. 6）② I need some cash in local currency. 我需要一些当地货币的现金。
[04:51.55]accessory 熟义 n. 附件，配件；配饰‖a. 辅助的，副的 示例 ① Pocket editions of the constitution are a must-have accessory for politicians. 袖珍版的宪法是政治家们的必备附件。（The Economist）② There are a range of furnishings and accessories for the home. 这有各种各样的家居装饰物及配件。
